# Copy to .env. Do not commit .env.
# Values left as __FILL_ME__ are treated as unset. The dashboard and the
# decision engine run offline with this file unchanged:
#   cp .env.example .env && docker compose up --build

# Listen port for `python -m src.app.main`. Compose publishes 8000.
# If that port is taken, the process exits and tells you to set PORT.
# PORT=8000

# sandbox (default) opens the local demo without an API key.
# production requires TRADEFLOW_API_KEY of 16+ characters and fails closed.
TRADEFLOW_ENV=sandbox

# Optional UN Comtrade subscription key. The preview works with no key.
# When set, it is sent as Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key and is never logged.
# COMTRADE_API_KEY=

# Optional CNY per 1 USD, supplied by you. Leave this unset to flag USD
# quotes instead of treating them as CNY. This file does not contain a rate.
# TRADEFLOW_USD_CNY_RATE=

# numpy (default) | cupy | rocm | gpu | auto
# cupy/rocm request a ROCm CuPy backend and fall back to NumPy if it cannot
# be imported. This repository has not recorded an AMD GPU measurement.
TRADEFLOW_SOLVER_BACKEND=numpy

# Optional AMD tokenfactory or any OpenAI-compatible vLLM endpoint.
# The decision engine does not call this unless a real key replaces __FILL_ME__.
# With a real key the probe lists models and sends one short chat completion.
# Evidence is written to results/amd_endpoint_evidence.json (gitignored).
#   python scripts/verify_amd_endpoint.py
#   python scripts/verify_amd_endpoint.py --no-chat   # models list only
# Default model for a new call. The committed 348-call log used
# Qwen3.8-Flash-Next; set VLLM_MODEL to that name to select it again.
VLLM_BASE_URL=https://developer.amd.com.cn/radeon/api/v1
VLLM_API_KEY=__FILL_ME__
VLLM_MODEL=Gemma-4-31B-IT

# Nebius Token Factory + NVIDIA Nemotron: the desk's quote reader. It names
# evidence spans and a class; it never sets a price. Unset leaves the rule
# reader only, and nothing is accepted automatically.
# TRADEFLOW_LLM_API_KEY=
# TRADEFLOW_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.tokenfactory.nebius.com/v1
# Desk reader model. Default: nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b. Ultra costs more:
# TRADEFLOW_LLM_MODEL=nvidia/Nemotron-3-Ultra-550b-a55b
# Model for the dashboard "Read this quote" live reading on Token Factory (default: the Super model).
# TRADEFLOW_DASHBOARD_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b
# Optional third hop on NVIDIA's hosted endpoint. Opens only after Nebius fails.
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# Tavily Search API: the "Web evidence" card (cited public pages for a product
# or a supplier). Reference only, never a price. Unset: the card says it is
# not configured. TRADEFLOW_WEB_EVIDENCE_OFFLINE=1 switches it off.
# TAVILY_API_KEY=
# TRADEFLOW_WEB_EVIDENCE_OFFLINE=

# Optional Evolus email-drafting adapter. Not required to run the demo.
EVOLUS_API_KEY=__FILL_ME__
EVOLUS_APP_ID=__FILL_ME__

# Live supplier desk. Leave the mailbox blank to run without intake.
# SQLite file. On Render's free plan this disk does not survive spin-down.
# TRADEFLOW_DESK_DB=

# IMAP poller. Starts only when host, username, and password are all set.
# Gmail app passwords use SSL on port 993. TLS certificate checks stay on.
# IMAP_SSL=0 is the loopback test fixture only. Other hosts are refused.
# IMAP_HOST=
# IMAP_PORT=993
# IMAP_USERNAME=
# IMAP_PASSWORD=
# IMAP_SSL=1
# IMAP_POLL_SECONDS=60
# IMAP_LOOKBACK_DAYS=14

# Optional Gmail API read. Drafts are created only when GMAIL_DRAFTS=1.
# The desk never calls the Gmail send method.
# GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=
# GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# GMAIL_DRAFTS=

# Approved sends reach SMTP only when DESK_SMTP_SEND=1 and the SMTP
# variables below are set. Otherwise approval stays on this desk.
# DESK_SMTP_SEND=
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=465
# EMAIL_USERNAME=
# EMAIL_PASSWORD=

# Desk solver budget. Integers. The auction path is separate.
# Every desk read and write needs TRADEFLOW_API_KEY above, in sandbox and in production.
# The sandbox demo token does not read the desk.
# [2026-10-24] Named operator keys are an additional credential, stored only as
# SHA-256 hashes in the desk database (schema version 2, table desk_users).
# Issue, list, and revoke them with scripts/manage_users.py; the raw secret is
# shown exactly once at issue time. A revoked key is refused like an unknown one
# on the next request, and a request made with a named key records
# "user:<id>:<label>" inside the audit chain entry, so the chain answers who
# acted. The shared TRADEFLOW_API_KEY still works and records "env-key" —
# it is shared, so it names nobody.
# TRADEFLOW_CHAIN_KEY is the HMAC key for the desk audit chain. It is never stored in the database.
# Desk sends refuse to start when it is unset. TRADEFLOW_CHAIN_KEY_ID names that key (default primary).
# TRADEFLOW_CHAIN_KEYS is id:secret pairs of retired keys, separated by commas.
# TRADEFLOW_CHAIN_ANCHOR is an optional file path or http(s) URL that stores the chain head
# outside the database. If it is unset, verify reports anchor not configured, and tail truncation
# is detectable only with an anchor.
# Migration is POST /api/v1/desk/deals/{id}/migrate. A restart does not migrate.
# A round-5 chain (empty key_id, HMAC without key_id) verifies with TRADEFLOW_CHAIN_KEY.
# After an anchor outage, POST /api/v1/desk/deals/{id}/reanchor rewrites that deal's head.
# TRADEFLOW_APPROVAL_PUBKEY is the Ed25519 public key (64 hex chars) that desk sends must be
# signed by (python -m src.desk.approval_signing keygen / sign). Pinning a key makes a signed
# approval REQUIRED: unsigned sends are refused, and a signature from any other key is refused.
# The matching private key never reaches the server; it turns HMAC tamper-evidence into
# human-level non-repudiation.
# TRADEFLOW_REQUIRE_SIGNED_APPROVAL forces the policy either way ("required" / "optional").
# Unset, TRADEFLOW_ENV=production implies required, and a production desk with no pinned key
# refuses every send rather than accepting an unsigned boolean as a human approval.
# The same key and policy cover supplier address changes (TRADEFLOW_REQUIRE_ADDRESS_SIGNATURE).
# An address change redirects the next counter, so on a desk with one shared API key it must
# be signed, not asserted by a JSON boolean:
#   python -m src.desk.approval_signing sign-address --key <key> --deal <id> --supplier <id> --address <email>
# TRADEFLOW_REQUIRE_ADDRESS_SIGNATURE=
# TRADEFLOW_MAX_REQUEST_BYTES caps the request body before it is buffered (default 1048576).
# A larger body is refused with 413 instead of being read into memory first.
# TRADEFLOW_APPROVAL_PUBKEY=
# TRADEFLOW_REQUIRE_SIGNED_APPROVAL=
# TRADEFLOW_MAX_REQUEST_BYTES=
# TRADEFLOW_CHAIN_KEY=
# TRADEFLOW_CHAIN_KEY_ID=
# TRADEFLOW_CHAIN_KEYS=
# TRADEFLOW_CHAIN_ANCHOR=
# DESK_N_SAMPLES=5000
# DESK_N_GRID=20
